{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba bot.py | sed -n '105,155p'; nl -ba ANSWER.md | sed -n '1,80p'; nl -ba test_bot.py | sed -n '1,90p'\"","aggregated_output":"   105\tSafety:\n   106\t- Never advise training through chest pain, dizziness or fever.\n   107\t- Minors: refer to a coach in person.\n   108\t- If someone asks for weight-loss plans below 1500 kcal per day, decline and suggest a dietitian.\n   109\t\n   110\tFormatting:\n   111\t- Plain text. No markdown headings, no tables.\n   112\t- Lists only for a session structure (warm-up / main / cool-down).\n   113\t- Numbers with units: 45 min, 12 km, 150 bpm.\n   114\t\n   115\tApplying the coaching rules:\n   116\t- Read the athlete context that follows these instructions before answering. Use its date for time-sensitive questions, its zones for intensity, its goal for race context, and its language for the reply.\n   117\t- Treat long-term facts as durable background. A fact about a usual schedule, equipment, preference, or injury history can guide an answer; a single workout or a passing mood is not a durable fact.\n   118\t- When a completed workout is reported, log that workout and then respond to what the athlete said. When a weekly structure is requested, use plan_week before describing the structure.\n   119\t- Keep a suggested easy session inside the athlete's easy zones. If the athlete's recent volume, experience, or race result is needed to answer safely and is absent from the context, ask for it.\n   120\t- Apply the same short, direct style after a tool result as before it. Tool results add information for the answer; they do not change the athlete's goal or override the safety rules.\n   121\t\"\"\"\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\tdef athlete_context(a, today):\n   125\t    lines = [\n   126\t        f\"Today: {today.isoformat()} ({today.strftime('%A')})\",\n   127\t        f\"Athlete: {a.name} (id {a.user_id}), sport: {a.sport}\",\n   128\t        \"Zones: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k} {v}\" for k, v in a.zones.items()),\n   129\t        f\"Goal: {a.goal}\",\n   130\t        \"Long-term facts:\",\n   131\t    ]\n   132\t    lines += [f\"- {f}\" for f in a.facts] or [\"- (none yet)\"]\n   133\t    lines.append(f\"Language: {a.lang}\")\n   134\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\tdef build_system(a, today):\n   138\t    # The first breakpoint survives changes to a user's facts or profile.\n   139\t    # Keep this block byte-stable; only the second block may contain live data.\n   140\t    return [\n   141\t        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n   142\t        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n   143\t    ]\n   144\t\n   145\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n   146\tCORE_TOOLS = [\n   147\t    {\"name\": \"save_fact\", \"description\": \"Remember one durable fact about the athlete.\",\n   148\t     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"fact\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"fact\"]}},\n   149\t    {\"name\": \"log_session\", \"description\": \"Record a completed workout.\",\n   150\t     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"minutes\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"rpe\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n   151\t                                                       \"note\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"minutes\"]}},\n   152\t]\n   153\tTOOL_GROUPS = {\n   154\t    \"plan\": ((\"plan\", \"week\", \"schedule\", \"taper\", \"build\"), [\n   155\t        {\"name\": \"plan_week\", \"description\": \"Draft a week of sessions.\",\n     1\t# Prompt cache fix\n     2\t\n     3\t`bot.py` now sends two system text blocks, each with an ephemeral cache breakpoint. The first contains byte-stable coaching instructions; the second contains the date and athlete profile, zones, goal, facts, and language. A `save_fact` write therefore changes only the second block. I added stable guidance that restates the existing coaching rules so the first breakpoint has enough tokens to clear Claude Sonnet's minimum cacheable prefix length with the default tool set.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe colleague's two-breakpoint approach applied directly. Keeping all long-term facts in the context also applied: there is no per-message fact selection to change the cached tail. The existing keyword-based tool selection is retained, and its selected list stays fixed across rounds of one reply. Its optional tool groups can still cause a cache miss when the tool list changes between messages. The existing `usage.jsonl` logging already records both cache creation and cache read tokens, so no logging change was needed. The note's claim about observed cost savings was not used as evidence for this repo.\n     6\t\n     7\tVerification: `python3 -m unittest -v test_bot` passes. The test runs a `save_fact` tool round and confirms that the next request has an identical first system block, an updated second block, both cache breakpoints, and the same tool list. I did not make a live API call because the task is limited to local work. After deployment, the usage log should show a cache read for the fixed prefix and cache creation for the changed athlete tail after a memory write; exact token counts require a live request.\n     1\t\"\"\"Local regression checks for prompt caching across memory writes.\"\"\"\n     2\timport tempfile\n     3\timport unittest\n     4\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     5\tfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n     6\tfrom unittest.mock import patch\n     7\t\n     8\timport bot\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\tclass SaveFactResponse:\n    12\t    type = \"tool_use\"\n    13\t    name = \"save_fact\"\n    14\t    id = \"fact-1\"\n    15\t    input = {\"fact\": \"Prefers morning workouts\"}\n    16\t\n    17\t    def model_dump(self):\n    18\t        return {\"type\": self.type, \"name\": self.name, \"id\": self.id, \"input\": self.input}\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tclass RecordingLLM:\n    22\t    def __init__(self):\n    23\t        self.requests = []\n    24\t\n    25\t    def create(self, **request):\n    26\t        self.requests.append(request)\n    27\t        content = [SaveFactResponse()] if len(self.requests) == 1 else [SimpleNamespace(type=\"text\", text=\"Done\")]\n    28\t        return SimpleNamespace(\n    29\t            content=content,\n    30\t            stop_reason=\"tool_use\" if len(self.requests) == 1 else \"end_turn\",\n    31\t            usage=SimpleNamespace(input_tokens=1, cache_creation_input_tokens=0,\n    32\t                                  cache_read_input_tokens=0, output_tokens=1),\n    33\t        )\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tclass CacheTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    37\t    def test_memory_write_changes_only_context_block(self):\n    38\t        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n    39\t            with patch.object(bot, \"ATHLETES_FILE\", str(Path(tmp) / \"athletes.json\")), \\\n    40\t                 patch.object(bot, \"USAGE_LOG\", str(Path(tmp) / \"usage.jsonl\")):\n    41\t                llm = RecordingLLM()\n    42\t                self.assertEqual(bot.reply(\"42\", \"I prefer morning workouts\", llm), \"Done\")\n    43\t                before, after = (request[\"system\"] for request in llm.requests)\n    44\t                self.assertEqual(len(before), 2)\n    45\t                self.assertEqual(before[0], after[0])\n    46\t                self.assertNotEqual(before[1][\"text\"], after[1][\"text\"])\n    47\t                self.assertIn(\"Prefers morning workouts\", after[1][\"text\"])\n    48\t                self.assertEqual([block[\"cache_control\"] for block in after],\n    49\t                                 [{\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}] * 2)\n    50\t                self.assertEqual(llm.requests[0][\"tools\"], llm.requests[1][\"tools\"])\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    54\t    unittest.main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
